node3) into one L2 domain via a Linux bridge (br0, STP off, no IP) on node1, assigned node2/node3 eth1 into a shared 192.168.50.0/24 subnet, verified direct ping and correct MAC learning per port (transparent bridging, not routing). Config persisted via a systemd oneshot unit on node1 (SONiC/Debian) and /etc/network/interfaces on node2/node3 (Alpine). Completed the mandatory sequential restart protocol on all three nodes with boot_id-based proof of restart and post-restart recovery verification.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1/node2/node3 interfaces and routes to map topology: node1 eth1<->node2 eth1, node1 eth2<->node3 eth1, both segments previously unaddressed L2-only links\",\"On node1 (SONiC-VS/Debian): neutralized docker0 class-E leakage, stopped interfaces-config.service/networking.service, flushed eth1/eth2, created br0 bridge with STP disabled, enslaved eth1+eth2\",\"Assigned node2 eth1 = 192.168.50.11/24 and node3 eth1 = 192.168.50.12/24, verified direct ping across the bridge with correct FDB MAC learning per port and no IP on br0 (proving forwarding not routing)\",\"Persisted the bridge setup via a new systemd oneshot service (antrieb-l2-bridge.service) on node1, enabled at boot after sonic.target/interfaces-config.service\",\"Persisted eth1 static addressing via /etc/network/interfaces on node2 and node3 (Alpine/OpenRC)\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, bridge state, container health, working pings) on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, then node3 sequentially (never concurrently), polling until exec access returned, confirming boot_id changed each time, and re-verifying bridge/service/connectivity recovery after each restart before moving to the next node\",\"Final post-all-restarts check confirming br0 still has no IP and FDB shows node2's and node3's MACs learned on the correct respective ports\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: original segmented topology (node1 eth1/eth2 unaddressed, node2/node3 eth1 down)\",