... to 030ffac9...; post-restart bridge auto-recreated via systemd unit, all SONiC containers active, cross-node ping succeeded\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bfe89e0fa2c24368\",\"cmd-197dd808cb974a00\",\"cmd-d36d709731e9497f\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed from 208921d8... to 7f2c37ac...; eth1 static IP persisted and ping to node3 succeeded post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6edb47f190194655\",\"cmd-6ecf76a508014da6\",\"cmd-15019f8aa96a4660\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed from 384aa966... to 02f40386...; eth1 static IP persisted and ping to node2 succeeded post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final verification: L2 domain and bridging behavior intact after all three sequential restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-571cb089eac74b07\"],\"summary\":\"FDB shows node2's and node3's MACs learned on the correct respective bridge ports (eth1/eth2); br0 has no IP address, confirming node1 forwards frames transparently rather than routing\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Joined node1's two segments (eth1↔node2, eth2↔node3) into one L2 domain via a Linux bridge (br0, STP off, no IP) on node1, assigned node2/node3 eth1 into a shared 192.168.50.0/24 subnet, verified direct ping and correct MAC learning per port (transparent bridging, not routing). Config persisted via a systemd oneshot unit on node1 (SONiC/Debian) and /etc/network/interfaces on node2/node3 (Alpine). Completed the mandatory sequential restart protocol on all three nodes with boot_id-based proof of restart and post-restart recovery verification.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1/node2/node3 interfaces and routes to map topology: node1 eth1<->node2 eth1, node1 eth2<->node3 eth1, both segments previously unaddressed L2-only links","On node1 (SONiC-VS/Debian): neutralized docker0 class-E leakage, stopped interfaces-config.service/networking.service, flushed eth1/eth2, created br0 bridge with STP disabled, enslaved eth1+eth2","Assigned node2 eth1 = 192.168.50.11/24 and node3 eth1 = 192.168.50.12/24, verified direct ping across the bridge with correct FDB MAC learning per port and no IP on br0 (proving forwarding not routing)","Persisted the bridge setup via a new systemd oneshot service (antrieb-l2-bridge.service) on node1, enabled at boot after sonic.target/interfaces-config.service","Persisted eth1 static addressing via /etc/network/interfaces on node2 and node3 (Alpine/OpenRC)","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, bridge state, container health, working pings) on all three nodes","Restarted node1, node2, then node3 sequentially (never concurrently), polling until exec access returned, confirming boot_id changed each time, and re-verifying bridge/service/connectivity recovery after each restart before moving to the next node","Final post-all-restarts check confirming br0 still has no IP and FDB shows node2's and node3's MACs learned on the correct respective ports"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: original segmented topology (node1 eth1/eth2 unaddressed, node2/node3 eth1 down)","command_ids":["cmd-fbdf8ac9467d47a0","cmd-c4823c0580c84122","cmd-dc33a9e2fb564ac4","cmd-e74b332d80b54c11"],"summary":"Showed node1's eth1/eth2 as separate link-local-only interfaces, node2/node3 eth1 down, confirming two distinct segments prior to bridging"},{"requirement":"SONiC pre-config cleanup (docker0 de-neutralized, reconcilers stopped) before bridging","command_ids":["cmd-347c6f92112e484a"],"summary":"Removed docker0's class-E IP and stopped interfaces-config/networking services on node1 per SONiC reference guidance"},{"requirement":"Single L2 domain created with node1 forwarding (bridge), not routing","command_ids":["cmd-d36a1a98084c4d82","cmd-e115d4aec46741ee","cmd-5a57935d0b614b3e","cmd-0864ee5873924877","cmd-229394406af742e4"],"summary":"br0 created enslaving eth1+eth2 in forwarding state; node2/node3 addressed into shared 192.168.50.0/24; successful ping node2->node3 across the bridge; FDB shows per-port MAC learning; br0 carries no IP, confirming L2 forwarding not L3 routing"},{"requirement":"Configuration persists across reboot","command_ids":["cmd-e7d47be68b3b4509","cmd-e2017427ae46433e","cmd-81c761d0a6c747d2"],"summary":"Installed and enabled antrieb-l2-bridge.service on node1 (recreates bridge at boot); added static eth1 stanzas to /etc/network/interfaces on node2 and node3"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline on all nodes","command_ids":["cmd-9cce98f425954a59","cmd-f6b850bd7cc94395","cmd-5a384b737428405d"],"summary":"Captured boot_id, bridge forwarding state, SONiC container health on node1, and working cross-segment pings from node2/node3 before any restart"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-ed42bf93feb3449c","cmd-db597e5e638346c2","cmd-c65aa564ed68416a","cmd-806527059fac451a"],"summary":"Reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; boot_id changed from 1f515f97... to 030ffac9...; post-restart bridge auto-recreated via systemd unit, all SONiC containers active, cross-node ping succeeded"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-bfe89e0fa2c24368","cmd-197dd808cb974a00","cmd-d36d709731e9497f"],"summary":"Reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed from 208921d8... to 7f2c37ac...; eth1 static IP persisted and ping to node3 succeeded post-restart"},{"requirement":"node3 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-6edb47f190194655","cmd-6ecf76a508014da6","cmd-15019f8aa96a4660"],"summary":"Reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed from 384aa966... to 02f40386...; eth1 static IP persisted and ping to node2 succeeded post-restart"},{"requirement":"Final verification: L2 domain and bridging behavior intact after all three sequential restarts","command_ids":["cmd-571cb089eac74b07"],"summary":"FDB shows node2's and node3's MACs learned on the correct respective bridge ports (eth1/eth2); br0 has no IP address, confirming node1 forwards frames transparently rather than routing"}]},"ttft_ms":2614,"type":"result","duration_ms":338153,"uuid":"56342f12-2a99-4eb6-81ac-17e9404fdbfa","ttft_stream_ms":1819,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":2613,"queued_turn_count":0}
